---
import {
  runtimeRows,
  nativeRuntime,
  memoryEvidence,
  irEvidence,
  highestObserved,
  percent,
  mib,
} from '../lib/evidence';
const lc = nativeRuntime.find((r) => r.suite === 'LoCoMo')!;
const lme = nativeRuntime.find((r) => r.suite === 'LongMemEval-S')!;
const suites = [...memoryEvidence, ...irEvidence];
const ms = (n: number | null) =>
  n === null ? 'Not recorded' : n.toFixed(2) + ' ms';
---

<p class="bench-host">
  <strong>Measured host:</strong> Apple M4 Pro · 24 GiB RAM · macOS 27.0 ARM64.
  CPU utilization and energy were not recorded.
</p>
<div class="metric-key">
  <span>
    <i class="metric-key-native" aria-hidden="true"></i>Blue: measured instantKV
    footprint and response time
  </span>
  <span>
    <i class="metric-key-best" aria-hidden="true"></i>Green: highest observed
    retrieval score in this suite
  </span>
</div>
<div
  class="table-scroll metrics-scroll"
  role="region"
  aria-label="Retrieval quality, RAM and response latency for every completed eval"
  tabindex="0"
>
  <table class="evidence-table runtime-table">
    <caption>
      All complete retrieval runs · RSS in MiB · query latency in milliseconds
    </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Eval / provider</th>
        <th scope="col">Recall@10 ↑</th>
        <th scope="col">nDCG@10 ↑</th>
        <th scope="col">Sampled RAM ↓</th>
        <th scope="col">p50 ↓</th>
        <th scope="col">p95 ↓</th>
        <th scope="col">p99 ↓</th>
        <th scope="col">Failed / limited ↓</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {suites.map((suite) =>
        runtimeRows
          .filter((row) => row.suite === suite.name)
          .map((row, index) => (
            <tr
              class:list={{
                'native-runtime': row.provider === 'instantKV',
                'suite-first': index === 0,
              }}
            >
              <th scope="row">
                <a href={row.raw}>{row.suite}</a>
                <span class="runtime-provider">{row.provider}</span>
                <small>
                  {suite.count.toLocaleString('en-US')} scored ·{' '}
                  {row.repetitions} {row.repetitions === 1 ? 'pass' : 'passes'}
                </small>
              </th>
              <td
                class:list={{ 'observed-best': highestObserved(row, 'recall') }}
              >
                <strong>{percent(row.recall)}%</strong>
                {highestObserved(row, 'recall') && (
                  <small>Highest observed</small>
                )}
              </td>
              <td
                class:list={{ 'observed-best': highestObserved(row, 'ndcg') }}
              >
                <strong>{percent(row.ndcg)}%</strong>
                {highestObserved(row, 'ndcg') && (
                  <small>Highest observed</small>
                )}
              </td>
              <td class="footprint-cell">
                <strong>{mib(row.rss)}</strong>
                <small>MiB · sampled RSS</small>
              </td>
              <td class="response-cell">{row.latency.p50.toFixed(2)}</td>
              <td class="response-cell response-p95">
                <strong>{row.latency.p95.toFixed(2)}</strong>
                <small>ms · query p95</small>
              </td>
              <td class="response-cell">{row.latency.p99.toFixed(2)}</td>
              <td>
                <strong>
                  {row.failures} / {row.truncated}
                </strong>
                <small>Failed / truncated</small>
                {row.reduced > 0 && (
                  <small>{row.reduced.toLocaleString('en-US')} reduced</small>
                )}
              </td>
            </tr>
          )),
      )}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="chart-note">
  Absent providers have no complete published run: LongMemEval-S Supermemory is
  incomplete; BEIR SQLite is not run. Query time is retrieval only; it excludes
  model inference. Blue emphasizes the native measurements, not a proven
  efficiency ratio. RAM process scopes and transports differ. Full memory
  timings reflect shared host load; BEIR controls are separately recorded runs.
  Highest observed scores are not significance claims.
</p>
<div class="resource-summary" aria-label="Native retrieval resource summary">
  <div>
    <span>LoCoMo / Rust server</span>
    <strong>
      {mib(lc.rss)} <small>MiB</small>
    </strong>
    <p>
      {percent(lc.recall)}% Recall@10 at {lc.latency.p95.toFixed(2)} ms query
      p95.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <span>LongMemEval-S / Rust server</span>
    <strong>
      {mib(lme.rss)} <small>MiB</small>
    </strong>
    <p>
      {percent(lme.recall)}% Recall@10 at {lme.latency.p95.toFixed(2)} ms query
      p95.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <span>Retrieval model requirement</span>
    <strong>None</strong>
    <p>No embedding model or model API in the memory engine.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<details class="runtime-details">
  <summary>More metrics: writes, startup, storage and throughput</summary>
  <p class="chart-note">
    Writes have different commit guarantees. Throughput is records divided by
    ingestion time for BEIR, or summed write-request time for the memory suites.
    It excludes query work and is not a concurrent query-throughput test.
    Supermemory's full-memory database size is cumulative across corpus scopes;
    others show the largest individual corpus database.
  </p>
  <div
    class="table-scroll"
    role="region"
    aria-label="Recorded storage and ingestion metrics"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <table class="evidence-table runtime-table detail-table">
      <caption>
        Additional recorded metrics; — means not recorded, not zero
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Eval / provider</th>
          <th scope="col">Database</th>
          <th scope="col">Write p95</th>
          <th scope="col">Startup p95</th>
          <th scope="col">Write throughput</th>
          <th scope="col">Binary</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {runtimeRows.map((row) => (
          <tr class:list={{ 'native-runtime': row.provider === 'instantKV' }}>
            <th scope="row">
              {row.suite}
              <span class="runtime-provider">{row.provider}</span>
            </th>
            <td>
              {row.disk === null ? '—' : mib(row.disk) + ' MiB'}
              <small>{row.diskScope}</small>
            </td>
            <td>
              {row.writeP95 === null ? '—' : ms(row.writeP95)}
              <small>{row.writeUnit}</small>
            </td>
            <td>{row.startupP95 === null ? '—' : ms(row.startupP95)}</td>
            <td>
              {row.writeThroughput === null
                ? '—'
                : row.writeThroughput.toFixed(1) + ' records/s'}
            </td>
            <td>{row.binary === null ? '—' : mib(row.binary) + ' MiB'}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h3 class="subsection-title">What the resource boundary includes</h3>
  <ul class="resource-boundaries">
    <li>
      <strong>instantKV:</strong> native Rust server, fresh database per corpus.
      RSS excludes the benchmark runner.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>SQLite FTS5:</strong> Python runner, interpreter and in-process
      adapter. No HTTP hop.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Supermemory local:</strong> server and descendants, including its
      embedding runtime. Full LoCoMo retains corpus scopes in one suite server.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Host:</strong> Apple M4 Pro, 24 GiB RAM, macOS 27.0 ARM64.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Not recorded:</strong> CPU utilization, CPU time, energy, separate
      index bytes and concurrent query throughput. RSS samples do not measure
      true peak RAM.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="/benchmark-data/full-retrieval/runtime-metrics.json"
  >
    Raw resource samples and derivation ↗
  </a>
</details>
<section class="native-resource-chart" aria-labelledby="native-resources-title">
  <header class="chart-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Native Rust process / complete retrieval sets</p>
      <h3 id="native-resources-title">The footprint beside the score</h3>
    </div>
    <span class="eyebrow">Lower resource use is better</span>
  </header>
  <div class="native-resource-labels" aria-hidden="true">
    <span>Full eval</span>
    <span>Sampled RAM / linear 0–32 MiB</span>
    <span>Query p95 / linear 0–50 ms</span>
  </div>
  {nativeRuntime.map((row) => (
    <div class="native-resource-row">
      <div>
        <strong>{row.suite}</strong>
        <small>{percent(row.recall)}% Recall@10</small>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="native-resource-track">
          <span style={`width:${(row.rss / 1024 ** 2 / 32) * 100}%`}></span>
        </div>
        <strong>{mib(row.rss)} MiB</strong>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="native-resource-track latency">
          <span style={`width:${(row.latency.p95 / 50) * 100}%`}></span>
        </div>
        <strong>{row.latency.p95.toFixed(2)} ms</strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  ))}
  <p class="chart-note">
    Each row uses its own complete eval workload. ArguAna's long queries have
    688 work-limit hits; the faster corpus timings do not guarantee the same
    speed for all tasks.
  </p>
</section>
